# A copy effect's exception is a copiable value (CR 707.9b): Thespian's Stage is a copy of an Island "except it has this
# ability", so Vesuva entering as a copy of that Stage-Island (CR 707.2) is an Island with the Stage's copy ability too. On turn
# 7 the Vesuva-Island uses it to become a copy of Bot2's Plains. The real Island has no such ability: the refusal, beside the
# Vesuva's activation, shows it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Thespian's Stage
Sol Ring
Island
Vesuva
Forest x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Thespian's Stage.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Thespian's Stage.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Thespian's Stage.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Island; Ability: becomes)
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Vesuva.Play
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Island#3.Tapped = true
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate(Ability: becomes)
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#3.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Plains; Ability: becomes)
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Sol Ring; Island; Island; Plains
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Subtypes = Plains
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Tapped = true
